ransform) pipelines giving RGD users integrated access to a wide variety of data to support their research efforts. RGD also offers a growing suite of innovative tools for querying, analyzing and visualizing this data making it a valuable resource for researchers worldwide.","CategoryLinkCount":1,"Section":[{"ObtainedBy":"ext_links","Tags":["related_data"],"SectionLinkCount":1,"Linklist":{"Link":[{"ObtainedBy":"ext_links","PublicationDate":"08-04-2025","LinkProvider":{"Name":"Europe PMC"},"RelationshipType":{"Name":"IsReferencedBy"},"Source":{"Type":{"Name":"literature"},"Identifier":{"ID":"30595499","IDScheme":"PMID"}},"Target":{"Type":{"Name":"dataset"},"Identifier":{"ID":"https://rgd.mcw.edu/rgdweb/report/reference/main.html?id=598117333","IDScheme":"URL","IDURL":"https://rgd.mcw.edu/rgdweb/report/reference/main.html?id=598117333"},"Title":"Lysosomal Signaling Licenses Embryonic Stem Cell Differentiation via Inactivation of Tfe3.","Publisher":{"Name":"Rat Genome Database"}}}]}}]}]}}